INT. DEEP-SPACE HAULER, CARGO BAY 3 - SHIP'S NIGHT

Stacked containers. Amber work lights. A thin layer of frost on the deck plates. The air recyclers wheeze.

CAPTAIN LUCIAN ASANTE-BROOKS, fifties, stands at a manifest console. FIRST MATE YUKI TANABE-REYES, thirties, runs a scanner along a container seam. CARGO MASTER BORIS ZIELINSKI, forties, big and tired, drags a crowbar. MEDIC ANJALI VERMA, thirties, hugs a trauma kit. A STOWAWAY, fifteen, sits cross-legged on a crate, arms wrapped round his knees. And the ship's AI, a disembodied voice named PILOT, hums through the wall speakers.

LUCIAN
Boris, open it.

BORIS
It's sealed from the inside.

YUKI
That's impossible.

ANJALI
Then who sealed it?

PILOT (V.O.)
Captain, thermal sensors indicate a heat signature in Container Seventeen.

LUCIAN
How warm?

PILOT (V.O.)
Thirty-seven degrees Celsius.

Yuki lowers her scanner. Boris sets his crowbar against the seam. Anjali edges away from the container, closer to the stowaway. The boy watches it with wide, unblinking eyes.

STOWAWAY
Don't open it.

LUCIAN
Who are you?

STOWAWAY
Please, don't.

BORIS
Captain, the lock's cooling.

YUKI
It's venting. Pressure's equalising.

PILOT (V.O.)
Warning. Structural integrity of Container Seventeen has been compromised.

The seam splits. A hiss of white vapour floods the deck, Boris staggers back, Yuki fires a flare, Anjali drags the boy behind a crate, and Lucian draws his sidearm. The door swings open.

Inside, curled on a bed of packing foam, a figure raises its head. It has the boy's face.
